hadiths[230]{hadithnumber,text}:
"23629","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from Sulayman ya'ni al-A'mash from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah from al-Mustawrid from Silah from Hudhayfah, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he would say in his bowing: Glory to my Lord the Most Great, and in his prostration: Glory to my Lord the Most High; and he never passed a verse of mercy but stood at it and asked, nor a verse of punishment but sought refuge from it."
"23630","Hushaym narrated to us, al-A'mash informed us from Abu Wa'il from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, come to a refuse heap of a people, and he urinated standing, then he called for water, so I brought it to him, and he performed ablution and wiped over his khuffs."
"23631","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Mansur from Abu Wa'il from Hudhayfah that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he stood at night, would brush his mouth with the siwak."
"23632","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Muslim ibn Nudhayr from Hudhayfah: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took hold of the muscle of my shin or his shin, and said: This is the place of the izar; if you refuse then lower; if you refuse then the izar has no right in what is below the ankles."
"23633","Sufyan narrated to us from Abd al-Malik from Rib'i from Hudhayfah, he said: He ya'ni the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he went to his bed, placed his right hand under his cheek and said: Lord, protect me from Your punishment on the Day You resurrect or gather Your servants."
"23634","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Za'idah from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Rib'i ibn Hirash from Hudhayfah that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Follow the two after me, Abu Bakr and Umar."
"23635","Sufyan narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, Shaqiq narrated to us from Hudhayfah that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to a refuse heap of a people and urinated standing, so I went to move away from him, and he brought me forward until Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And a word fell upon my father."
"23636","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us from Ibrahim from Hammam from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No talebearer shall enter Paradise."
"23637","Jarir narrated to us from Mansur from Abu Wa'il from Hudhayfah, he said: It reached him that Abu Musa would urinate in a bottle and say: The Children of Israel, when urine touched one of them, he would cut its place. Hudhayfah said: I wish that your companion would not impose this strictness; I saw myself walking with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and we ended at a refuse heap, and he stood urinating as one of you urinates; I went to turn away from him, and he said: Come near; so I drew near him until I was at his heels."
"23638","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us from Khuthaymah from Abu Hudhayfah, Abu Abd al-Rahman said: His name is Salamah ibn al-Haytham ibn Suhayb, from the companions of Ibn Mas'ud, from Hudhayfah, he said: When we were present with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, over food, we would not put our hands until the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, began and put his hand; and we were present with him over food, and a girl came as if pushed, and she went to put her hand in the food, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took her hand; and a Bedouin came as if pushed, and he went to put his hand in the food, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took his hand; then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Satan deems food lawful if the name of Allah is not mentioned over it, and he brought this girl to make lawful through her, so I took her hand; and he brought this Bedouin to make lawful through him, so I took his hand; by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, his hand is in my hand along with their hands, ya'ni Satan."
"23639","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us from Shaqiq from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Dajjal is blind in the left eye, abundant in hair; with him are a garden and a fire, so his fire is a garden and his garden is a fire."
"23640","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Abu Malik al-Ashja'i narrated to us from Rib'i ibn Hirash from Hudhayfah, he said: This nation was favored over all nations by three: the earth was made for it a purification and a mosque, and its rows were made like the rows of the angels. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would say this. And I was given these verses at the end of al-Baqarah from a treasure under the Throne; no prophet before me was given them. Abu Mu'awiyah said: All of it from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"23641","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Abu Malik al-Ashja'i narrated to us from Rib'i ibn Hirash from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: All good is charity."
"23642","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Abu Malik al-Ashja'i narrated to us from Rib'i ibn Hirash from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari and from Hudhayfah, they said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There was a man among those before you who dealt in sins; when death came to him he said to his family: When I die, burn me, then grind me, then scatter me in the sea on a windy day. When he died they did so. Allah Almighty gathered him in His hand and said to him: What carried you to do what you did? He said: Fear of You. He said: I have forgiven you."
"23643","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Abu Malik al-Ashja'i narrated to us from Rib'i ibn Hirash from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: From what people have attained of the first prophethood: If you do not feel shame, do whatever you wish."
"23644","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us from Zayd ibn Wahb from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to us two hadiths; I have seen one of them and I await the other. He narrated to us that trust descended into the root of the hearts of men, then the Quran descended, and they learned from the Quran and learned from the Sunnah. Then he narrated to us about the removal of trust, saying: A man sleeps a sleep, and trust is taken from his heart, and its trace remains like the trace of a speck; then trust is taken from his heart, and its trace remains like the trace of a blister, like an ember you rolled upon your foot, you see it raised and there is nothing in it. He said: Then he took pebbles and rolled them upon his foot. He said: Then people trade and hardly anyone fulfills trust until it is said: Among Banu so-and-so is a trustworthy man; until it is said of a man: How strong he is, how witty, how intelligent, and there is not in his heart a mustard seed of faith. A time came upon me when I did not care whom I traded with; if he was a Muslim his religion would return it to me, and if he was a Christian or a Jew his agent would return it to me; as for today, I would not trade with any of you except so-and-so and so-and-so."
"23645","Waki' narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us from Zayd ibn Wahb from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to us two hadiths; I saw one of them and I await the other, then he mentioned its meaning."
"23646","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from Sulayman, he said: I heard Zayd ibn Wahb narrating from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to us two hadiths, then he mentioned the hadith."
"23647","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us from Zayd ibn Wahb, he said: Hudhayfah entered the mosque, and there was a man praying near the doors of Kindah, not completing bowing nor prostration; when he finished, Hudhayfah said to him: How long is this your prayer? He said: For forty years. He said to him: You have not prayed for forty years, and if you died with this prayer you would die upon other than the fitrah upon which Muhammad was created, upon him be prayer and peace. He said: Then he turned to him teaching him, saying: A man may lighten his prayer yet complete the bowing and the prostration."
"23648","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us from Shaqiq from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Count for me how many utter Islam. We said: O Messenger of Allah, do you fear for us while we are between six hundred to seven hundred? He said: You do not know; perhaps you will be tested. He said: So we were tested until a man among us would not pray except secretly."
"23649","Ismail narrated to us from Yunus from Humayd ibn Hilal or from other than him from Rib'i ibn Hirash from Hudhayfah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: There will be rulers who lie and wrong; whoever believes them in their lies and helps them in their wronging is not from me nor am I from them, nor will he come to me at the Hawd; and whoever does not believe them in their lies and does not help them in their wronging is from me and I am from him, and he will come to me at the Hawd."
"23650","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah from al-Mustawrid ibn Ahnaf from Silah ibn Zufar from Hudhayfah, he said: I prayed with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one night. He opened al-Baqarah and recited until he reached the top of a hundred; I said: He will bow; then he went on until he reached two hundred; I said: He will bow; then he went on until he completed it; I said: He will bow; then he opened Surah Al Imran until he completed it; I said: He will bow; then he opened Surah al-Nisa and recited it; then he bowed and said in his bowing: Glory to my Lord the Most Great; his bowing was like his standing; then he prostrated, and his prostration was like his bowing, and he said in his prostration: Glory to my Lord the Most High; and when he passed a verse of mercy he asked, and when he passed a verse with punishment he sought refuge, and when he passed a verse with transcendence of Allah Almighty he glorified."
"23651","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us from Layth from Bilal from Shutayr ibn Shakal and from Silah ibn Zufar and from Sulayk ibn Mishal al-Ghifari, they said: Hudhayfah came out to us while we were talking, and he said: You speak words we used to count as hypocrisy in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"23652","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Shu'bah, he said: Qatadah narrated to us from Abu Mijlaz from Hudhayfah about one who sits in the middle of the circle, he said: Cursed upon the tongue of the Prophet or the tongue of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"23653","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Mis'ar, Wasil narrated to me from Abu Wa'il from Hudhayfah that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, met him on one of the roads of Madinah, and he reached out to him. I said: I am junub. He said: The believer does not become impure."
"23654","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Shu'bah from Mansur from Abdullah ibn Yasar from Hudhayfah that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not say: What Allah wills and so-and-so wills; say: What Allah wills, then so-and-so wills."
"23655","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Yusuf ya'ni Ibn Suhayb narrated to us from Musa ibn Abi al-Mukhtar from Bilal al-Absi, he said: Hudhayfah said: No tents after tents that were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Badr; nothing is repelled from them as is repelled from the people of these tents, and no people intend them evil except there comes to them what distracts them from them."
"23656","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Jahm from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed the fear prayer at Dhi Qarad, a land of the land of Banu Sulaym; the people lined behind him in two rows, a row facing the enemy and a row behind him; he prayed with the row next to him one rak'ah, then these stepped back to the positions of those and those to the positions of these, and he prayed with them another rak'ah."
"23657","Waki' narrated to us from Sufyan from Ash'ath ibn Abi al-Sha'tha from al-Aswad ibn Hilal from Tha'labah ibn Zahdam al-Hanzali, he said: We were with Sa'id ibn al-As at Tabaristan, and he said: Which of you prayed the fear prayer with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? Hudhayfah said: I. Sufyan said: And he described the like of the hadith of Ibn Abbas and Zayd ibn Thabit."
"23658","Waki' narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from al-Hakam from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade wearing silk and dibaj and vessels of gold and silver, and said: It is for them in this world and for us in the Hereafter."
"23659","Waki' narrated to us from Habib ibn Sulaym al-Absi from Bilal ibn Yahya al-Absi from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade al-na'y."
"23660","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Rib'i ibn Hirash from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he went to his bed, said: In Your name, O Allah, I die and live; and when he woke he said: Praise be to Allah who gave us life after He caused us to die, and to Him is the resurrection."
"23661","Waki' narrated to us from Sufyan from Abu Ishaq from Silah ibn Zufar from Hudhayfah, he said: Al-Sayyid and al-Aqib came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, send with us your trustworthy man; and Waki' once said: A trustworthy man. He said: I will send with you a trustworthy man, truly trustworthy. People aspired to it, and he sent Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah."
"23662","Waki' narrated to us from Sufyan from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir from Rib'i ibn Hirash, he said: One who never lied to me narrated to me ya'ni Hudhayfah, he said: Jibril, peace be upon him, met the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was at the stones of al-Mira', and he said: Your nation recite the Quran in seven ahruf; whoever of them recites upon a harf, let him recite as he learned and not turn back from it. My father said: And Ibn Mahdi said: Among your nation is the weak; whoever recites upon a harf, let him not shift from it to another, disliking it."
"23663","Waki' narrated to us from Sufyan from al-A'mash from Abu Wa'il from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood among us a standing, and he left nothing to be before the Hour but mentioned it in that standing of his; whoever memorized it memorized it, and whoever forgot it forgot it. Hudhayfah said: I see things I had been made to forget, and I recognize them as a man recognizes the face of a man who was absent from him, he sees him and recognizes him; and Waki' once said: And he saw him and recognized him."
"23664","Waki' narrated to us from Ibn Abi Layla from a shaykh called Hilal from Hudhayfah, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about everything, even about wiping pebbles. He said: Once, or leave."
"23665","Waki' narrated to us from Sufyan from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from a freedman of Rib'i from Rib'i from Hudhayfah, he said: We were sitting with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: I do not know how long I shall remain among you, so follow the two after me, and he pointed to Abu Bakr and Umar; and hold to the covenant of Ammar; and whatever Ibn Mas'ud narrates to you, believe him."
"23666","Waki' narrated to us, Abu al-Umays narrated to us from Abu Bakr ibn Amr ibn Utbah from a son of Hudhayfah from his father that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he supplicated for a man, it befell him and befell his child and his grandchild."
"23667","Waki' narrated to us, Razin ibn Habib al-Juhani narrated to us from Abu al-Ruqad al-Absi from Hudhayfah, he said: A man would speak a word in the time of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and thereby become a hypocrite, and I hear it from one of you today in the gathering ten times."
"23668","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Malik al-Ashja'i Sa'd ibn Tariq informed us, Rib'i ibn Hirash narrated to us from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I know better what is with the Dajjal than the Dajjal himself; with him are two rivers flowing, one in the sight of the eye white water, and the other in the sight of the eye blazing fire; if one of you reaches it, let him come to the river he sees as fire, let him close his eyes, then lower his head and drink, for it is cool water; and the Dajjal is wiped in the left eye, over it a thick film, written between his eyes: Disbeliever, every believer reads it, literate and illiterate."
"23669","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Malik narrated to us from Rib'i ibn Hirash from Hudhayfah that he came from Umar. He said: When we sat to him yesterday, he asked the companions of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Which of you heard the saying of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about tribulations? They said: We heard it. He said: Perhaps you mean the tribulation of a man in his family and wealth. They said: Yes. He said: I am not asking about that; those are expiated by prayer, fasting, and charity; but which of you heard the saying of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the tribulations that surge like the waves of the sea? The people held back, and I thought he meant me. I said: I. He said to me: You, may Allah keep your father for Allah. I said: Tribulations are presented to hearts like a mat; whichever heart rejects them, a white dot is marked in it, and whichever heart drinks them in, a black dot is marked in it, until the heart becomes upon two hearts: white like al-Safa, no tribulation harms it as long as the heavens and earth endure, and the other black murky like an overturned cup, and he tilted his palm, recognizing no good nor rejecting evil except what is drunk of its desire."
"23670","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from Adi ibn Thabit from Abdullah ibn Yazid from Hudhayfah that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed me of what will be until the Hour rises; there is nothing of it except I asked him about it, except I did not ask him what will expel the people of Madinah from Madinah."
"23671","Bahz and Abu al-Nadr said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Humayd, he is Ibn Hilal, narrated to us, Abu al-Nadr said in his hadith: Humayd ya'ni Ibn Hilal narrated to me, Nasr ibn Asim al-Laythi narrated to us, he said: I came to al-Yashkuri among a group of Banu Layth. He said: Who are the people? We said: Banu Layth. We asked him and he asked us, then we said: We came to you to ask you about the hadith of Hudhayfah. He said: We came back with Abu Musa, and beasts became dear in Kufah, so I and a companion of mine sought permission from Abu Musa, and he permitted us; we arrived at Kufah early in the day. I said to my companion: I will enter the mosque, and when the market stands I will come out to you. I entered the mosque, and there was a circle as if their heads were cut off, listening to the hadith of a man. I stood over them. A man came and stood beside me. I said: Who is this? He said: Are you a Basran? I said: Yes. He said: I knew; if you were a Kufan you would not ask about this; this is Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman. I drew near him and heard him say: People used to ask the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about good, and I asked him about evil, and I knew good would not precede me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, after this good will there be evil? He said: O Hudhayfah, learn the Book of Allah and follow what is in it, three times. I said: O Messenger of Allah, after this evil will there be good? He said: A truce upon smoke, and a community upon impurities. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the truce upon smoke? He said: Hearts of peoples will not return to what they were upon. I said: O Messenger of Allah, after this good will there be evil? He said: A blind deaf tribulation, upon it callers at the gates of Fire; and that you die O Hudhayfah biting upon a root is better for you than following any of them."
"23672","Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Kathir Abu al-Nadr narrated to us from Rib'i ibn Hirash, he said: I went to Hudhayfah at al-Mada'in on the nights people marched to Uthman, and he said: O Rib'i, what did your people do? I said: Which of their matters do you ask about? He said: Who went out of them to this man? I named men among those who went out to him. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever parts from the community and belittles leadership, he will meet Allah Almighty with no face for him with Him."
"23673","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Kathir ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, Rib'i ibn Hirash narrated to us from Hudhayfah that he came to him at al-Mada'in, then he mentioned it."
"23674","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us from Asim from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: I came upon Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman while he was narrating about the night Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was taken by night, saying: So I went forth or we went forth until we came upon Bayt al-Maqdis, and they did not enter it. I said: Nay, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered it that night and prayed in it. He said: What is your name O bald one, for I know your face and do not know your name? I said: I am Zirr ibn Hubaysh. He said: What is your knowledge that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed in it that night? I said: The Quran informs me of that. He said: Whoever speaks by the Quran succeeds; recite. So I recited: Glory to Him who took His servant by night from al-Masjid al-Haram. He said: I did not find that he prayed in it. He said: O bald one, do you find he prayed in it? I said: No. He said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not pray in it that night; if he had prayed in it, prayer in it would have been prescribed upon you as prayer in the Ancient House was prescribed upon you; by Allah, they did not leave al-Buraq until the gates of heaven were opened for them, and they saw Paradise and Fire and the promise of the Hereafter altogether, then they returned as they began. He said: Then he laughed until I saw his molars. He said: And they narrate that he tied it lest it flee, but it was only subjected to him by the Knower of the unseen and the seen. I said: O Abu Abdullah, what beast is al-Buraq? He said: A white tall beast, thus its stride is the extent of sight."
"23675","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Rib'i ibn Hirash from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was likely when he took his bed at night to place his right hand under his right cheek, then say: O Allah, in Your name I live and in Your name I die; and when he woke at night he said: Praise be to Allah who gave me life after He caused me to die, and to Him is the resurrection."
"23676","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us from Bakr ibn Amr from Abu Abd al-Malik from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The excellence of the house near the mosque over the distant house is like the excellence of the warrior over the one who sits back."
"23677","Abu Asim narrated to us, Kathir ibn Abi Kathir al-Tamimi narrated to us, Rib'i ibn Hirash narrated to us, my father said: And Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Kathir narrated to us from Rib'i that he came to Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman at al-Mada'in visiting him and visiting his sister. Hudhayfah said: What did your people do O Rib'i, did anyone go out? Yes, and I named a number, and that was in the time of the people's going out to Uthman. Hudhayfah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever goes out from the community and belittles leadership, he will meet Allah with no face for him with Him."
"23678","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us from Muhammad from Abu Ubaydah ibn Hudhayfah from Hudhayfah, he said: A man begged in the time of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the people withheld; then a man gave him, and the people gave. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever institutes a good and it is followed, he has its reward and from the rewards of those who follow him without decreasing from their rewards anything; and whoever institutes an evil and it is followed, upon him is its burden and from the burdens of those who follow him without decreasing from their burdens anything."
"23679","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us from Abu Wa'il from Hudhayfah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Peoples will come to me at the Hawd, and they will be snatched away from me; I will say: Lord, my companions, my companions; and it will be said to me: You do not know what they innovated after you."
"23680","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Salih ya'ni Ibn Kaysan from Ibn Shihab, he said: Abu Idris A'idhullah ibn Abdullah al-Khawlani said: I heard Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman say: By Allah, I am the most knowledgeable of people of every tribulation to be between me and the Hour; not that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, told me something of that he confided to me that he did not tell others, but the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said while narrating in a gathering I was in, he was asked about tribulations, while counting tribulations, among them three that leave nothing, like the winds of summer, among them small and among them great. Hudhayfah said: That group all went except me."
"23681","Fazarah ibn Amr narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to us, then he mentioned the like of it."
"23682","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, and I heard it myself from Harun, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to me that Amr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to him that the freedman of Shurahbil ibn Hasanah narrated to him that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani and Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Eat whatever your bow returns to you."
"23683","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us from Amr ibn Shu'ayb that he narrated to him that the freedman of Shurahbil ibn Hasanah narrated to him that he heard Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani and Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Eat whatever your bow returns to you."
"23684","Waki' narrated to us from Isra'il, he said: Abu Ishaq said from Abdullah ibn Ghalib from Hudhayfah, he said: The master of the children of Adam on the Day of Resurrection is Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"23685","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Abdullah ibn Ghalib from Hudhayfah, he said: The master of the children of Adam on the Day of Resurrection is Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"23686","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Abdullah ibn Ghalib from Hudhayfah, he said: The master of the children of Adam on the Day of Resurrection is Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"23687","Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Abdullah ibn Ghalib from Hudhayfah, he said: The master of the children of Adam on the Day of Resurrection is Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"23688","Ismail ibn Umar and Khalaf ibn al-Walid said: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ya'ni Ibn Za'idah narrated to us from Ikrimah ibn Ammar from Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Du'ali, he said: Abd al-Aziz brother of Hudhayfah said, Hudhayfah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when a matter distressed him, prayed."
"23689","Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, a cousin of Hudhayfah narrated to me from Hudhayfah, he said: I stood with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one night, and he recited the seven long ones in seven rak'ahs; when he raised his head from bowing he said: Allah hears him who praises Him, then he said: Praise be to Allah, Possessor of dominion, might, pride and greatness; his bowing was like his standing, and his prostration was like his bowing; then he finished, and my feet had almost broken."
"23690","Sulayman al-Hashimi narrated to us, Ismail ya'ni Ibn Ja'far informed us, Amr ya'ni Ibn Abi Amr informed me from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ashhal from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, you shall enjoin good and forbid evil, or Allah will soon send upon you punishment from Him, then you will supplicate Him and He will not answer you."
"23691","Sulayman narrated to us, Ismail informed us, Amr narrated to me from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ashhal from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Hour will not rise until you kill your imam and fight with your swords, and your dwellings are inherited by your worst ones."
"23692","Sulayman narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, Amr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ashhali narrated to me from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Hour will not rise until the happiest of people with worldly life is Luka' ibn Luka'."
"23693","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard al-A'mash from Abu Wa'il from Hudhayfah, he said: The Dajjal was mentioned at the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: I fear the trial of some of you more with me than the trial of the Dajjal; none will be saved from what is before it except he will be saved from it; and no trial has been made since the world began, small or great, except for the trial of the Dajjal."
"23694","Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan Abu Sa'id al-Ahwal narrated to us from al-A'mash, Ibrahim narrated to me for about sixty years from Hammam ibn al-Harith, he said: A man passed by Hudhayfah, and it was said: This one carries reports to the rulers. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say, or the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No slanderer shall enter Paradise."
"23695","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Iyad ibn Laqit narrated to us, he said: I heard my father mention from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about the Hour, and he said: Its knowledge is with my Lord, none manifests it at its time but He; but I will inform you of its conditions and what will be before it: before it is tribulation and harj. They said: O Messenger of Allah, tribulation we know, what is harj? He said: In the language of Abyssinia, killing; and estrangement will be cast among people, and hardly anyone will know anyone."
"23696","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from Mansur from Rib'i, he said: I heard a man at the funeral of Hudhayfah say: I heard the owner of this bed say: No harm to me in what I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; if you fight one another I will enter my house, and if entered upon me I will say: Here, bear my sin and your sin."
"23697","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: We came to Hudhayfah and said: Guide us to the nearest of people to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in guidance, conduct and loyalty, that we may take from him and hear from him. He said: The nearest of people to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in guidance, conduct and manner was Ibn Umm Abd until he disappears from me into his house; and the preserved companions of Muhammad, upon him be prayer and peace, knew that Ibn Umm Abd is among the nearest of them to Allah in nearness."
"23698","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us from al-A'mash from Abu Wa'il from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood among us a standing, and he left nothing in it to be before the Hour but he mentioned it; whoever memorized it memorized it, and whoever forgot it forgot it. I see a thing and remember it as a man recognizes the face of a man absent from him, then he sees him and recognizes him."
"23699","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us from Mansur from Ibrahim from Hammam from Hudhayfah, he said: A man used to carry reports to Uthman, reports from Hudhayfah. Hudhayfah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: No slanderer shall enter Paradise, ya'ni a talebearer."
"23700","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from al-A'mash from Sa'id ibn Ubaydah from Silah ibn Zufar from Hudhayfah that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he passed a verse of fear, sought refuge, and when he passed a verse of mercy, asked; and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he bowed, said: Glory to my Lord the Most Great, and when he prostrated, said: Glory to my Lord the Most High."
"23701","Abdallah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Razin al-Juhani narrated to us, Abu al-Ruqad narrated to me, he said: I went out with my master while I was a boy, and I was handed over to Hudhayfah, and he was saying: A man would utter a word at the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and thereby become a hypocrite, and now I hear it from one of you in a single sitting four times. You shall command what is right, and you shall forbid what is wrong, and you shall urge one another to good, or Allah will sweep you all away with a punishment, or He will appoint your worst over you, then your best will supplicate and it will not be answered for you."
"23702","Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaida narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, he said: I heard Hudhayfah say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he stood for tahajjud, would rub his mouth with the siwak."
"23703","Yahya ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniyya narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Hudhayfah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Do not drink from gold nor from silver, and do not wear silk and dibaj, for it is theirs in this world and yours in the Hereafter."
"23704","Affan narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Thabit ibn Wadia, that a man of Banu Fazara brought the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, some lizards he had trapped. He began turning over one of the lizards before him and said: A nation was transformed. And to the best of my knowledge he said: I do not know what it did, and I do not know whether this is from them. And Shuba said: I heard it. And Husayn said, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Hudhayfah, he said, and he mentioned something similar to this. He said: He neither commanded it nor forbade anyone."
"23705","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu al-Tufayl, he said: I set out, I and Amr ibn Sulay, until we came to Hudhayfah. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: This clan of Mudar will not leave a righteous servant of Allah on the earth but it will tempt him and destroy him, until Allah overtakes it with soldiers from His servants, and humiliates it until it cannot protect the tail of a mountain path."
"23706","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Hudhayfah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The distance between my Hawd is as between Ayla and Mudar. Its vessels are more, or he said, like the number of the stars of the sky. Its water is sweeter than honey, whiter than milk, colder than snow, and better scented than musk. Whoever drinks from it will never thirst afterwards."
"23707","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Hudhayfah, he said: What is between the two ends of the Hawd of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is as Ayla and Mudar. Then he mentioned it. And thus Yunus said, as Affan said."
"23708","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu Nadra, from Qays, he said: I said to Ammar: What do you think of this deed of yours that you did in the matter of Ali, an opinion you held, or something the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, covenanted to you? He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not covenant to us anything he did not covenant to people in general, but Hudhayfah informed me from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Among my Companions are twelve hypocrites, eight of them will not enter Paradise until the camel passes through the eye of the needle."
"23709","Ismail ibn Umar narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Hudhayfah, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not pray in Bayt al-Maqdis, and had he prayed in it, the prayer of your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would have been prescribed upon you."
"23710","Muhammad ibn Abdallah ibn al-Zubayr and Abu Nuaym narrated to us, they said: al-Walid, meaning Ibn Jumay, narrated to us. Abu Nuaym said, from Abu al-Tufayl, like Jumay. Abu al-Tufayl narrated to us, he said: There occurred between Hudhayfah and a man of the people of al-Aqaba what occurs between people, and he said: I adjure you by Allah, how many were the companions of al-Aqaba? The people said to him: Tell him since he asked you. He said: We were told that they were fourteen. And Abu Nuaym said: The man said: We were told they were fourteen. He said: If you were among them, and Abu Nuaym said, among them, then the people were fifteen. And I testify by Allah that twelve of them are at war with Allah and His Messenger in the life of this world and on the Day the witnesses stand. Abu Ahmad said: The witnesses. And he counted for us three. They said: We did not hear the crier of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and we did not know what the people intended. Abu Ahmad said in his hadith: And he had been in a lava field, and he walked and said to the people: The water is little, so let none precede me to it. Then he found people who had preceded him, and he cursed them that day."
"23711","Muhammad ibn Abdallah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Sad ibn Aws narrated to us, from Bilal al-Absi, from Hudhayfah, he said: No tents after tents that were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, were more defended against harm than tents placed in this spot. And he said: You today, O Arabs, commit matters that at the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, were outright hypocrisy."
"23712","Hasan narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salama, from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: People will come out of the Fire after the Fire has scorched them. They will be called al-Jahannamiyyun."
"23713","Hasan and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Uthman al-Batti, from Nuaym. Affan said in his hadith: Ibn Abi Hind, from Hudhayfah, he said: I leaned the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, against my chest, and he said: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, Hasan said: seeking the Face of Allah, and is sealed with it, will enter Paradise. And whoever fasts a day seeking the Face of Allah, and is sealed with it, will enter Paradise. And whoever gives charity seeking the Face of Allah, and is sealed with it, will enter Paradise."
"23714","Hashim narrated to us, Mahdi narrated to us, from Wasil al-Ahdab, from Abu Wail, from Hudhayfah, that it reached him that a man spreads reports. Hudhayfah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: No tale-bearer will enter Paradise."
"23715","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdala narrated to us, from Zirr, from Hudhayfah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The Quran was revealed in seven ahruf."
"23716","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Abdallah ibn Abd al-Rahman, one of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, from Hudhayfah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, you shall command what is right and forbid what is wrong, or He will send a people against you, then you will supplicate Him and it will not be answered for you."
"23717","Abu al-Mughira narrated to us, Safwan narrated to us, al-Safr ibn Nusayr al-Azdi and others narrated to us, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, we were in evil, and Allah removed that evil and brought good by your hands, so is there after the good any evil? He said: Yes. He said: What is it? He said: Trials like pieces of the dark night, following one another, coming to you ambiguous like the faces of cows; you will not know which from which."
"23718","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Maysara ibn Habib, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Hudhayfah, he said: My mother asked me: How long since your meeting with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: I said to her: Since such-and-such. He said: Then she reproached me and reviled me. He said: I said to her: Leave me, for I will go to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and pray Maghrib with him, then I will not leave him until he seeks forgiveness for me and for you. He said: So I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and prayed Maghrib with him. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Isha, then turned away, and I followed him. An intruder appeared before him and conversed with him privately, then went away, and I followed him. He heard my voice and said: Who is this? I said: Hudhayfah. He said: What is the matter with you? So I told him the matter, and he said: May Allah forgive you and your mother. Then he said: Did you see the intruder who appeared before me just now? He said: I said: Yes. He said: He is an angel among the angels who had never descended to the earth before this night. He asked permission of his Lord to greet me and to give me glad tidings that al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the leaders of the youth of Paradise, and that Fatima is the leader of the women of Paradise, may Allah be pleased with them."
"23719","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Ibn Abi al-Safar, from al-Shabi, from Hudhayfah, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and prayed with him Zuhr and Asr and Maghrib and Isha, then I followed him while he intended to enter one of his rooms. He stood while I was behind him as if speaking to someone. He said, then he said: Who is this? I said: Hudhayfah. He said: Do you know who was with me? I said: No. He said: Jibril came to give me glad tidings that al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the leaders of the youth of Paradise. He said: Hudhayfah said: So seek forgiveness for me and for my mother. He said: May Allah forgive you, O Hudhayfah, and your mother."
"23720","Abu Qatan narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, he said: A man passed, and they said: This is the informer of the rulers. Hudhayfah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: No qattat will enter Paradise."
"23721","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salama, narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdala, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was brought al-Buraq, and it is a white tall beast placing its hoof at the end of its glance. We did not leave its back, I and Jibril, peace be upon him, until we came to Bayt al-Maqdis. The gates of heaven were opened for us, and I saw Paradise and the Fire. Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman said: And he did not pray in Bayt al-Maqdis. Zirr said: I said to him: Yes, he did pray. Hudhayfah said: What is your name, O bald one, for I know your face and do not know your name? I said: I am Zirr ibn Hubaysh. He said: And how do you know that he prayed? I said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic says: Glory to Him Who took His servant by night from the Sacred Mosque to the Farthest Mosque, which We blessed around, that We might show him of Our signs. Indeed He is the Hearing, the Seeing. He said: Do you find that he prayed? Had he prayed, you would have prayed in it as you pray in the Sacred Mosque. Zirr said: And he tied the beast to the ring to which the prophets, peace be upon them, tie. Hudhayfah said: Would he fear that it would go away from him, though Allah had brought it to him?"
"23722","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdala narrated to us, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was brought al-Buraq. Then he mentioned its meaning. Hasan said in his hadith, meaning this hadith: And they both saw Paradise and the Fire. And Affan said: And the gates of heaven were opened for them, and he saw Paradise and the Fire."
"23723","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Yazid ibn Ziyad narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, he said: A youth of ours from the people of Kufa said to Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman: O Abu Abdallah, did you see the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and accompany him? He said: Yes, O son of my brother. He said: How did you act? He said: By Allah, we strove hard. He said: By Allah, had we met him, we would not have left him walking on the earth, and we would have carried him on our necks. Hudhayfah said: O son of my brother, by Allah, you saw us with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at al-Khandaq. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed part of the night, then turned to us and said: Which man will stand and look for us what the people did, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stipulating for him that he return, Allah will admit him to Paradise. But no man stood. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed part of the night, then turned to us and said: Which man will stand and look for us what the people did, then return, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stipulating for him the return, I ask Allah that he be my companion in Paradise. But no man of the people stood, with severe fear and severe hunger and severe cold. When none stood, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called me, and I had no choice but to stand when he called me. He said: O Hudhayfah, go and enter among the people and look what they do, and do not cause anything until you come to us. He said: So I went and entered among the people, while the wind and the soldiers of Allah did what they did; no pot settled for them, nor fire, nor building. Abu Sufyan ibn Harb stood and said: O Quraysh, let each man look who his companion is. Hudhayfah said: So I took the hand of the man beside me and said: Who are you? He said: I am so-and-so son of so-and-so. Then Abu Sufyan said: O Quraysh, by Allah, you have not awakened in an abode of stay. The steeds have perished, Banu Qurayza have failed us, there has reached us from them what we dislike, and we have met from this wind what you see. By Allah, no pot is steady for us, nor does a fire stand for us, nor does a building hold for us. So depart, for I am departing. Then he stood to his camel while it was hobbled, sat on it, then struck it, and it jumped on three legs. Its hobble was released only while it was standing. Had it not been for the covenant of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, not to cause anything until I came to him, had I wished I would have killed him with an arrow. Hudhayfah said: Then I returned to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was standing praying in a cloak of one of his wives, ornamented. When he saw me, he admitted me to his baggage and threw the edge of the cloak over me, then he bowed and prostrated while in it. When he gave salam, I told him the news. And Ghatafan heard of what Quraysh did and hastened to their lands."
"23724","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Hirash, he said: I was at the funeral of Hudhayfah, and a man of the people said: I heard this one, meaning Hudhayfah, say: I am not troubled by what I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. If you fight one another, I will look to the farthest house in my dwelling and enter it. If I am entered upon, I will say: Here, bear my sin and your sin, or my offense and your offense."
"23725","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, Ibn Hubayra narrated to us, that he heard Abu Tamim al-Jayshani say: Said informed me that he heard Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was absent from us one day and did not come out until we thought he would never come out. When he came out, he prostrated a prostration, and we thought his soul had been taken in it. When he raised his head, he said: My Lord, Blessed and Exalted, consulted me about my nation, what I should do with them. I said: Whatever You wish, my Lord, they are Your creation and Your servants. Then He consulted me a second time, and I said the same to Him. He said: I will not grieve you concerning your nation, O Muhammad. And He gave me glad tidings that the first of my nation to enter Paradise are seventy thousand, with every thousand seventy thousand, with no reckoning upon them. Then He sent to me and said: Supplicate and you will be answered, and ask and you will be given. I said to His messenger: Will my Lord grant my request? He said: He sent me to you only to grant you. My Lord the Mighty and Majestic has granted me, and no pride, and forgiven me my past and future sins while I walk alive healthy. He granted me that my nation will neither hunger nor be overcome. He granted me al-Kawthar, and it is a river of Paradise flowing into my Hawd. He granted me might and victory and terror traveling before my nation a month. He granted me that I am the first of the prophets to enter Paradise. He made spoils good for me and my nation, and permitted for us much of what was made strict upon those before us, and He placed upon us no hardship."
"23726","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from al-Mughira, from Abu Wail, from Ibn Masud, and Husayn, from Abu Wail, from Hudhayfah, they said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I am your predecessor over the Hawd, awaiting you. Men from you will be raised to me until, when I know them, they will be snatched away from me. I will say: My Lord, my companions, my companions. It will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you."
"23727","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I know better what is with the Dajjal than he does. With him is a burning fire, and Husayn once said, burning, and a river of cold water. Whoever of you reaches him, let him not perish by him. Let him close his eyes and fall into what he sees as fire, for it is a river of cold water."
"23728","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sufyan, meaning Ibn Uyayna, narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Ribi, from Hudhayfah, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I saw in a dream that I met one of the People of the Book, and he said: Good people you are, were it not that you say: What Allah wills and Muhammad wills. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I used to dislike it from you. So say: What Allah wills, then Muhammad wills."
"23729","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Mughira, from Hudhayfah, he said: There was in my tongue sharpness toward my family, which I did not extend to others. I mentioned that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Where are you from seeking forgiveness, O Hudhayfah? I seek Allah every day a hundred times and repent to Him."
"23730","He said: So I mentioned it to Abu Burda ibn Abi Musa, and he narrated to me from Abu Musa that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I seek Allah every day and night a hundred times and repent to Him."
"23731","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, he said: Hudhayfah said: The people most like in guidance and conduct and appearance to Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is Abdallah ibn Masud, from when he goes out until he returns. I do not know what he does in his house."
"23732","Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaida narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, he said: I was sitting with Hudhayfah, and Abdallah ibn Masud came. Hudhayfah said: The people most like in guidance and conduct to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from when he goes out of his house until he returns, and I do not know what he does with his family, is Abdallah ibn Masud. By Allah, the guarded ones among the Companions of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, knew that Abdallah is among the nearest of them to Allah in means on the Day of Resurrection."
"23733","Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdala informed us, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Hudhayfah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought al-Buraq, and it is a white tall beast placing its hoof at the end of its glance. He said: He and Jibril, peace be upon him, did not leave its back until they came to Bayt al-Maqdis. The gates of heaven were opened for them, and they both saw Paradise and the Fire. He said: And Hudhayfah said: And he did not pray in Bayt al-Maqdis. Zirr said: I said: Yes, he did pray. Hudhayfah said: What is your name, O bald one, for I know your face and do not know your name? He said: I said: I am Zirr ibn Hubaysh. He said: And how do you know, and do you find that he prayed? He said: I said: By the saying of Allah the Mighty and Majestic: Glory to Him Who took His servant, the verse. He said: And do you find that he prayed? Had he prayed in it, we would have prayed in it as we pray in the Sacred Mosque. And it was said to Hudhayfah: He tied the beast to the ring to which the prophets, peace be upon them, tied. Hudhayfah said: Would he fear that it would go away, though Allah had brought it to him?"
"23734","Affan narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, he said: I asked Sulayman, and he narrated to me from Sad ibn Ubayda, from al-Mustawrid, from Sila ibn Zufar, from Hudhayfah, that he prayed with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He would say in his bowing: Glory to my Lord the Mighty, and in his prostration: Glory to my Lord the Most High. He never passed a verse of mercy but he stopped and asked, nor a verse of punishment but he sought refuge."
"23735","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Yunus, meaning Ibn Abi Ishaq, narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Nuhayk al-Saluli, Hudhayfah narrated to us, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, come to the refuse heap of a people and urinate standing."
"23736","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Hudhayfah, that he said: What is between the two ends of the Hawd of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is as between Ayla and Mudar. Its vessels are more, or like the number of the stars of the sky. Its water is sweeter than honey, whiter than milk, colder than snow, and better scented than musk. Whoever drinks from it will never thirst afterwards, ever."
"23737","Affan narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abdallah ibn Yasar, from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Do not say: What Allah wills and so-and-so wills, but say: What Allah wills, then so-and-so wills."
"23738","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abu al-Bakhtari al-Tai, from Abu Thawr, he said: Uthman sent on the day of al-Jaraa with Said ibn al-As. He said: They went out to him and turned him back. He said: I was sitting with Abu Masud and Hudhayfah. Abu Masud said: I did not think he would return without blood being shed in it. Hudhayfah said: But I knew it would return on its heels without even a cupping-glass of blood being shed in it. I knew nothing of that but I knew it while Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was alive. Even a man becomes a believer in the morning, then in the evening nothing of it remains with him. And he is a believer in the evening and in the morning nothing of it remains with him. He fights his faction today, and Allah kills him tomorrow. His heart is inverted, his buttocks overtop him. He said: I said: His lower part? He said: His buttocks."
"23739","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Tharwan, from Amr ibn Hanzala, he said: Hudhayfah said: By Allah, Mudar will not leave a believing servant of Allah but they will tempt him or kill him, or Allah and the angels and the believers will strike them until they cannot protect the tail of a mountain path. A man said to him: Do you say this, O Abdallah, while you are a man of Mudar? He said: I say only what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said."
"23740","Affan narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, Abu Ishaq informed me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: We said to Hudhayfah: Tell us of a man near in demeanor and guidance to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that we may take from him. He said: I know none nearer in demeanor and guidance and conduct to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, until the wall of his house conceals him, than Ibn Umm Abd. And we did not hear this from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid. The guarded ones among the Companions of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, knew that Ibn Umm Abd is among the nearest of them to Allah the Mighty and Majestic in means."
"23741","Affan narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Walid ibn al-Ayzar, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Hudhayfah, with all of this."
"23742","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abu Rawq, Atiyya ibn al-Harith, narrated to us, Mukhmil ibn Dimath narrated to us, he said: I raided with Said ibn al-As. He said: He asked the people: Who of you witnessed the fear prayer with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: Hudhayfah said: I did. He prayed with one group of the people one raka, while a group faced the enemy. Then these went and stood at the place of their companions facing the enemy, and the other group came, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with them one raka, then gave salam. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had two rakas, and each group one raka."
"23743","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Ribi, he said: Uqba ibn Amr said to Hudhayfah: Will you not narrate to us what you heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say? He said: I heard him say: With the Dajjal, when he emerges, are water and fire. What people see as fire is cold water, and what people see as water is burning fire. Whoever of you reaches that, let him fall into what he sees as fire, for it is sweet cold water."
"23744","Hudhayfah said: And I heard him say: A man among those before you, an angel came to take his soul and said to him: Did you do any good? He said: I know none. It was said to him: Look. He said: I know nothing except that I traded with people and was lenient with them. I gave respite to the insolvent and overlooked the solvent. So Allah the Mighty and Majestic admitted him to Paradise."
"23745","He said: And I heard him say: A man was approached by death, and when he despaired of life, he bequeathed to his family: When I die, gather for me abundant thick firewood, then kindle a fire in it, until when it has eaten my flesh and reached my bone and burned it black, take it and scatter it in the sea. They did so. Allah the Mighty and Majestic gathered him to Himself and said to him: Why did you do that? He said: From fear of You. He said: So Allah forgave him. Uqba ibn Amr said: I heard him say that, and he was a grave-robber."
"23746","Abdallah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, and I heard it from Abdallah ibn Abi Shayba, Abu Usama narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Jumay, Abu al-Tufayl narrated to us, Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Nothing prevented me from witnessing Badr but that I went out, I and my father Husayl, and the disbelievers of Quraysh seized us and said: You intend Muhammad. We said: We intend only Medina. They took from us the covenant of Allah and His pact that we would return to Medina and not fight with him. So we came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and told him the news. He said: Go back. We fulfill their covenant, and we seek Allahs help against them."
"23747","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Farafisa narrated to us, a man narrated to me, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, that he came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: While I was praying, I heard a speaker say: O Allah, to You is all praise, to You is all dominion, in Your Hand is all good, to You returns all matter, its public and its secret. Worthy to be praised, indeed You are over all things Able. O Allah, forgive me all my past sins, protect me in what remains of my life, and grant me a pure deed You are pleased with from me. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: That is an angel who came to you teaching you the praise of your Lord."
"23748","Affan narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Muslim ibn Nudhayr, from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took the calf muscle of my leg, or the calf muscle of his leg. He said: The izar is here. If you refuse, then here. If you refuse, then there is no right for the izar in the ankles, or no right for the ankles in the izar."
"23749","Affan narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, al-Hakam narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla, that Hudhayfah was at al-Madain, and a dihqan brought him a cup of silver. He took it and threw it at him, and said: I did this only because I had forbidden him and he did not stop. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade me drinking in vessels of gold and silver, and silk and dibaj, and said: It is theirs in this world and yours in the Hereafter."
"23750","Ali ibn Abdallah narrated to us, Muadh, meaning Ibn Hisham, narrated to us, he said: I found in the book of my father in his handwriting, and I did not hear it from him, from Qatada, from Abu Mashar, from Ibrahim al-Nakhai, from Hammam, from Hudhayfah, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: In my nation are twenty-seven liars and impostors, among them four women. And I am the Seal of the Prophets, there is no prophet after me."
"23751","Affan narrated to us, Mahdi narrated to us, Wasil al-Ahdab narrated to us, from Abu Wail, from Hudhayfah, that it reached him about a man who spreads reports. Hudhayfah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: No tale-bearer will enter Paradise."
"23752","Affan narrated to us, Mahdi narrated to us, Wasil al-Ahdab narrated to us, from Abu Wail, from Hudhayfah, that he saw a man not completing bowing nor prostration. When he finished his prayer, Hudhayfah called him and said to him: For how long have you prayed this prayer? He said: I have prayed it for such-and-such. Hudhayfah said: You have not prayed, or he said: You have not prayed for Allah a prayer, Mahdi doubted, and I think he said: Had you died, you would have died upon other than the sunna of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"23753","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdala informed us, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: I took suhur, then set out to the mosque, and passed by the house of Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman. I entered upon him, and he ordered a milch camel and it was milked, and a pot and it was heated. Then he said: Come near and eat. I said: I intend fasting. He said: And I intend fasting. So we ate and drank, then we came to the mosque and the prayer was established. Then Hudhayfah said: Thus the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did with me. I said: After dawn? He said: Yes, it is dawn, except that the sun had not risen. He said: And between the house of Hudhayfah and the mosque is as between the mosque of Thabit and the garden of Hawt. And Hammad also said: And Hudhayfah said: Thus I did with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did with me."
"23754","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Walid Abu al-Mughira, or al-Mughira Abu al-Walid, narrate that Hudhayfah said: O Messenger of Allah, I am sharp of tongue, and most of that is against my family. He said: Where are you from seeking forgiveness? He said: I seek forgiveness in the day and night, or in the day, a hundred times."
"23755","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, a cousin of Hudhayfah narrated to me, from Hudhayfah, he said: I stood beside the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one night, and he recited the seven long suras in seven rakas. He said: When he raised his head from bowing, he said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, then he said: Praise be to Allah, Possessor of dominion and might and pride and greatness. His bowing was about like his standing, and his prostration about like his bowing. He finished his prayer while my legs had almost broken."
"23756","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abi Layla, he said: Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, he said: I went out with Hudhayfah to some of this Sawad, and he asked for water. A dihqan brought him a vessel of silver. He said: So he threw it at his face. He said: We said: Be quiet, be quiet. If we ask him, he will not narrate to us. He said: So we were quiet. He said: When it was after that, he said: Do you know why I threw it at his face? He said: We said: No. He said: I had forbidden him. He said: Then he mentioned the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Do not drink in vessels of gold. Muadh said: Do not drink in gold nor in silver, and do not wear silk nor dibaj, for they are theirs in this world and yours in the Hereafter."
"23757","Abu Muawiya narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Dajjal is blind in the left eye, with abundant hair. With him are a garden and a fire. His fire is a garden, and his garden is a fire."
"23758","Abu Muawiya and Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he stood at night, would rub his mouth. Ibn Numayr said: I said to al-Amash: With the siwak? He said: Yes."
"23759","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ubayda, from al-Mustawrid ibn al-Ahnaf, from Sila ibn Zufar, from Hudhayfah, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one night. He opened with al-Baqara. I said: He will bow at a hundred. He said: Then he went on. I said: He will pray it in one raka. Then he went on. I said: He will bow with it. Then he opened al-Nisa and recited it. Then he opened Al Imran and recited it, reciting at ease. When he passed a verse with glorification, he glorified. When he passed a request, he asked. When he passed seeking refuge, he sought refuge. Then he bowed and began to say: Glory to my Lord the Mighty. His bowing was about like his standing. Then he said: Allah hears whoever praises Him. Then he stood long, nearly as he bowed. Then he prostrated and said: Glory to my Lord the Most High. His prostration was near his standing."
"23760","Abd al-Rahman and Abu Nuaym narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, he said: We were with Hudhayfah, and it was said to him: So-and-so reports hadiths to Uthman. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: No qattat will enter Paradise."
"23761","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he went to his bed, said: O Allah, in Your Name I die and in Your Name I live. And when he awoke, he said: Praise be to Allah Who gave us life after He caused us to die, and to Him is the resurrection."
"23762","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Malik, and Ibn Jafar, Shuba narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from Ribi, from Hudhayfah. Ibn Jafar said: From the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Every good deed is charity."
"23763","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Ubayd ibn al-Mughira, from Hudhayfah, he said: I was a man sharp of tongue against my family. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I feared my tongue would admit me to the Fire. He said: Where are you from seeking forgiveness? I seek Allah in the day a hundred times. Abu Ishaq said: I mentioned it to Abu Burda, and he said: And I repent to Him."
"23764","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, some of our companions narrated to me, from Hudhayfah, that the polytheists seized him and his father, and took upon them that they would not fight them on the day of Badr. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Fulfill for them, and we seek Allahs help against them."
"23765","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Khaythama, from Abu Hudhayfah, from Hudhayfah, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and food was brought. A bedouin came as if driven, and went to take some. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took his hand. A girl came as if driven, and reached out. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took her hand. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When Satan found you unyielding, he came with the bedouin and the girl to make the food lawful when the name of Allah is not mentioned over it. In the Name of Allah, eat."
"23766","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla narrate that Hudhayfah asked for water, and a man brought him a vessel of silver. He threw it at him and said: I had forbidden him, but he refused to stop. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us to drink in vessels of gold and silver, and from wearing silk and dibaj, and said: It is theirs in this world and yours in the Hereafter."
"23767","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abu Hamza, a man of the Ansar, from a man of Banu Abs, from Hudhayfah, that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at night. When he entered the prayer, he said: Allah is Greater, Possessor of dominion and might and pride and greatness. He said: Then he recited al-Baqara. Then he bowed, and his bowing was about like his standing. He would say: Glory to my Lord the Mighty. Then he raised his head, and his standing was about like his bowing. He would say: To my Lord is praise, to my Lord is praise. Then he prostrated, and his prostration was about like his standing. He would say: Glory to my Lord the Most High, Glory to my Lord the Most High. Then he raised his head, and what is between the two prostrations was about like the prostration. He would say: My Lord, forgive me, My Lord, forgive me. He said: Until he recited al-Baqara and Al Imran and al-Nisa and al-Maida and al-Anam. It is Shuba who doubts about al-Maida and al-Anam."
"23768","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abu Hamza, a man of the Ansar, from a man of Banu Abs, from Hudhayfah, that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at night. When he entered the prayer, he said: Allah is Greater, Possessor of dominion and might and pride and greatness. He said: Then he recited al-Baqara. Then he bowed, and his bowing was about like his standing. He would say: Glory to my Lord the Mighty. Then he raised his head, and his standing was about like his bowing. He would say: To my Lord is praise, to my Lord is praise. Then he prostrated, and his prostration was about like his standing. He would say: Glory to my Lord the Most High, Glory to my Lord the Most High. Then he raised his head, and what is between the two prostrations was about like the prostration. He would say: My Lord, forgive me, My Lord, forgive me. He said: Until he recited al-Baqara and Al Imran and al-Nisa and al-Maida and al-Anam. It is Shuba who doubts about al-Maida and al-Anam."
"23769","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq narrate from Sila ibn Zufar, from Hudhayfah, that he said: The people of Najran came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Send to us a trustworthy man. He said: I will send to you a trustworthy man, truly trustworthy, truly trustworthy. He said: People vied for it. He said: So he sent Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah, may Allah be pleased with him."
"23770","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Muslim ibn Nudhayr, from Hudhayfah, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took the calf muscle of my leg, or the calf muscle of his leg, and said: The right of the izar is here. If you refuse, then here. If you refuse, then there is no right for the izar in the ankles, or no right for the ankles in the izar."
"23771","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Malik, meaning al-Ashjai, narrate from Ribi, from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Every good deed is charity."
"23772","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from his wife, from the sister of Hudhayfah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed us and said: O women, do you not have in silver what to adorn yourselves? Indeed, no woman among you who wears gold and displays it but she will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection."
"23773","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj narrated to us, they said: Shuba narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abdallah ibn Yasar, from Hudhayfah, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not say: What Allah wills and so-and-so wills, but say: What Allah wills, then so-and-so wills."
"23774","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from al-Tufayl, brother of Aisha by her mother, that a Jew saw in his dream, then he mentioned the hadith."
"23775","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said about the Dajjal: With him are water and fire. His fire is cold water, and his water is fire. So do not perish. Abu Masud said: And I heard it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"23776","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that a man died and entered Paradise. It was said to him: What did you do? He said: Whether he remembered or was reminded, he said: I traded with people. I gave respite to the insolvent and was lenient in coin or in payment. So he was forgiven. Abu Masud said: And I heard it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"23777","Abdallah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywa narrated to us, Bakr ibn Amr narrated to me, that Abu Abd al-Malik Ali ibn Yazid al-Dimashqi narrated to him, that it reached him from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: The excellence of the near house, meaning from the mosque, over the far house is like the excellence of the warrior over the sitter."
"23778","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Salim al-Muradi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Harim al-Azdi, from Abu Abdallah and Ribi ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, he said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: I do not know how long I will remain among you, so follow the two after me, pointing to Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both. Follow the guidance of Ammar and the covenant of Ibn Umm Abd, may Allah be pleased with them both."
"23779","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Mahdi, from Wasil al-Ahdab, from Abu Wail, he said: It was said to Hudhayfah: A man spreads reports. Hudhayfah said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: No tale-bearer will enter Paradise."
"23780","Muhammad ibn Adi narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, he said: Jundub said: When it was the day of al-Jaraa, and there was a man, he said: He said: By Allah, blood will be shed today. He said: The man said: No, by Allah. He said: Why did you not say: Yes, by Allah? He said: No, by Allah, it is the hadith of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he narrated it to me. He said: I said: By Allah, I see you an evil companion since today. You hear me swear, though you heard it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and do not forbid me. He said: Then I said: What is it to me and anger? He said: So I left anger and turned to ask him. And behold the man was Hudhayfah."
"23781","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Ashath, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, from Thalaba ibn Zahdam al-Yarbui, he said: We were with Said ibn al-As at Tabaristan, and he said: Which of you remembers the fear prayer with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? Hudhayfah said: He led us. We stood a row behind him and a row facing the enemy. He prayed with those next to him one raka, then they went to the ranks of those, and those came, and he prayed with them one raka, then gave salam to them."
"23782","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu al-Bakhtari, he said: Hudhayfah said: The Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asked him about good, and I asked him about evil. It was said: Why did you do that? He said: Whoever guards against evil falls into good."
"23783","Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he took his bed, said: O Allah, in Your Name I live and die. And when he stood, he said: Praise be to Allah Who gave us life after He caused us to die, and to Him is the resurrection."
"23784","Muammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Hudhayfah, he said: Bilal used to come to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was taking suhur, and I could see the places of my arrows. I said: After dawn? He said: After dawn, except that the sun had not risen."
"23785","Muammal narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Muslim, narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, from Abu Wail, from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Peoples will come to my Hawd. When I see them, they will be snatched away from me. I will say: O Lord, my companions, my companions. It will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you."
"23786","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Amr ibn Utba, from Ibn Hudhayfah. Misar said: And he once mentioned it from Hudhayfah, that the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, reaches a man and his son and his sons son."
"23787","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, al-Walid, meaning Ibn Jumay, narrated to us, Abu al-Tufayl narrated to us, from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out on the day of the raid of Tabuk. He said: It reached him that in the water he would come to there was little. He ordered a crier, and he called among the people that none should precede me to the water. He came to the water, and people had preceded him. So he cursed them."
"23788","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn al-Ayzar, he said: Hudhayfah said: I spent the night with the family of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood praying, with an edge of the quilt over him and over Aisha its edge, while she was menstruating and not praying."
"23789","Affan narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, Abu Ishaq informed us, he said: I heard Sila ibn Zufar, from Hudhayfah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to the people of Najran: I will send to you a trustworthy man, truly trustworthy. He said it more than twice. People vied for it. So he sent Abu Ubayda, may Allah be pleased with him."
"23790","Affan narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salama, narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Hudhayfah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I met Jibril at the stones of al-Mira. I said: O Jibril, I was sent to an unlettered nation, man and woman and boy and girl and aged elder who never reads a book at all. He said: The Quran was revealed in seven ahruf."
"23791","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, from Talha ibn Yazid al-Ansari, from Hudhayfah, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a night of Ramadan, and he stood praying. When he said takbir, he said: Allah is Greater, Possessor of dominion and might and pride and greatness. Then he recited al-Baqara, then al-Nisa, then Al Imran, not passing a verse of fright but he stopped at it. Then he bowed, saying: Glory to my Lord the Mighty, like as he stood. Then he raised his head and said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, our Lord, to You is praise, like as he stood. Then he prostrated, saying: Glory to my Lord the Most High, like as he stood. Then he raised his head and said: My Lord, forgive me, like as he stood. Then he prostrated, saying: Glory to my Lord the Most High, like as he stood. Then he raised his head and stood. He prayed only two rakas until Bilal came and announced the prayer to him."
"23792","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Asim ibn Bahdala, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: I said to Hudhayfah: At what hour did you take suhur with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: It is daytime, except that the sun had not risen."
"23793","Waki narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, he said: Hudhayfah asked a dihqan or a non-Arab for water, and he brought him a silver vessel. He threw it at him, then turned to the people offering an apology, and said: I did that with him deliberately, because I had forbidden him before this time. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us wearing dibaj and silk, and vessels of gold and silver, and said: It is theirs in this world, and it is ours in the Hereafter."
"23794","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Muslim ibn Nudhayr, from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took the calf muscle of my leg and said: This is the place of the izar. If you refuse, then lower than that. If you refuse, then there is no right for the izar in the ankles."
"23795","Waki narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilaba, he said: Abu Abdallah said to Abu Masud, or Abu Masud said to Abu Abdallah, meaning Hudhayfah: What did you hear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say about zajamu? He said: I heard him say: Evil is the mount of a man."
"23796","Waki narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth, from Hudhayfah, he said: I spent the night with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He stood and prayed in a garment, its edge over him and its edge over his family."
"23797","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood among us a station and told us of what will be until the Day of Resurrection. Whoever remembered it remembered it, and whoever forgot it forgot it."
"23798","Waki narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu Mijlaz, that a man sat in the middle of a circle of people. Hudhayfah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed, or he said: Cursed upon the tongue of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is he who sits in the middle of the circle."
"23799","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Sila ibn Zufar, from Hudhayfah, he said: al-Aqib and al-Sayyid came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Send with us a trustworthy man. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I will send with you a trustworthy man, trustworthy, trustworthy. He said: The Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, knelt for it upon their knees. He said: So he sent Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah, may Allah be pleased with him."
"23800","Waki narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: We said to Hudhayfah: Tell us of the nearest people in demeanor to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that we may take from him and hear from him. He said: The people most like in demeanor and conduct and guidance to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is Ibn Umm Abd."
"23801","Waki' narrated to us from Walid ibn Abdillah ibn Jumay' from Abu al-Tufayl from Hudhayfah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and news of shortage of water reached him, so he said: Let no one get ahead of me to the water."
"23802","Abdurrahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir from Rib'i ibn Hirash who said: One who never lied to me narrated to me, he said, and when he said 'one who never lied to me narrated to me' we thought he meant Hudhayfah, he said: Jibril met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the stones of al-Mira', and said: Among your ummah are the weak, so whoever recites upon one harf should not shift from it to another out of aversion to it."
"23803","Abdurrahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us from Abdulmalik ibn Umayr, the son of Hudhayfah's brother narrated to me from Hudhayfah who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night to pray with his prayer, so he began and recited a recitation neither silent nor loud, a fine recitation in which he measured out, letting us hear, he said: Then he bowed about as long as his standing, then he raised his head about as long as his bowing, and said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, then he said: Praise be to Allah, Lord of omnipotence, sovereignty, pride and greatness, until he finished at length, with a blackness of the night upon him, he said: Abdulmalik said: It is the voluntary night prayer."
"23804","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from al-A'mash, Shaqiq narrated to me, he said: I heard Hudhayfah, and Waki' from al-A'mash from Shaqiq from Hudhayfah, and Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us and said: I heard Hudhayfah, he said: We were sitting with Umar and he said: Which of you remembers the statement of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about tribulation, I said: I do, as he said it, he said: You are bold concerning it, I said: The tribulation of a man in his family, his wealth, his child and his neighbor is expiated by prayer, charity, enjoining right and forbidding wrong, he said: That is not what I mean, but the tribulation that surges like the waves of the sea, I said: There is no harm for you in it, O Commander of the Believers, between you and it is a closed door, he said: Will it be broken or opened, I said: Rather it will be broken, he said: Then it will never be closed again, we said: Did Umar know who the door was, he said: Yes, as he knows that before tomorrow there is a night, he said, and Waki' in his hadith said: Masruq said to Hudhayfah: O Abu Abdillah, did Umar know what he was told, we said: Did Umar know who the door was, he said: Yes, as he knows that before tomorrow there is a night, I told him a hadith with no confusion in it, so we were in awe of Hudhayfah to ask him who the door was, so we told Masruq and he asked him, and he said: The door is Umar."
"23805","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from al-A'mash, Shaqiq narrated to me, he said: I heard Hudhayfah, and Waki' from al-A'mash from Shaqiq from Hudhayfah, and Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us and said: I heard Hudhayfah, he said: We were sitting with Umar and he said: Which of you remembers the statement of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about tribulation, I said: I do, as he said it, he said: You are bold concerning it, I said: The tribulation of a man in his family, his wealth, his child and his neighbor is expiated by prayer, charity, enjoining right and forbidding wrong, he said: That is not what I mean, but the tribulation that surges like the waves of the sea, I said: There is no harm for you in it, O Commander of the Believers, between you and it is a closed door, he said: Will it be broken or opened, I said: Rather it will be broken, he said: Then it will never be closed again, we said: Did Umar know who the door was, he said: Yes, as he knows that before tomorrow there is a night, he said, and Waki' in his hadith said: Masruq said to Hudhayfah: O Abu Abdillah, did Umar know what he was told, we said: Did Umar know who the door was, he said: Yes, as he knows that before tomorrow there is a night, I told him a hadith with no confusion in it, so we were in awe of Hudhayfah to ask him who the door was, so we told Masruq and he asked him, and he said: The door is Umar."
"23806","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from al-A'mash, Shaqiq narrated to me, he said: I heard Hudhayfah, and Waki' from al-A'mash from Shaqiq from Hudhayfah, and Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us and said: I heard Hudhayfah, he said: We were sitting with Umar and he said: Which of you remembers the statement of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about tribulation, I said: I do, as he said it, he said: You are bold concerning it, I said: The tribulation of a man in his family, his wealth, his child and his neighbor is expiated by prayer, charity, enjoining right and forbidding wrong, he said: That is not what I mean, but the tribulation that surges like the waves of the sea, I said: There is no harm for you in it, O Commander of the Believers, between you and it is a closed door, he said: Will it be broken or opened, I said: Rather it will be broken, he said: Then it will never be closed again, we said: Did Umar know who the door was, he said: Yes, as he knows that before tomorrow there is a night, he said, and Waki' in his hadith said: Masruq said to Hudhayfah: O Abu Abdillah, did Umar know what he was told, we said: Did Umar know who the door was, he said: Yes, as he knows that before tomorrow there is a night, I told him a hadith with no confusion in it, so we were in awe of Hudhayfah to ask him who the door was, so we told Masruq and he asked him, and he said: The door is Umar."
"23807","Yahya narrated to us from Shu'bah, Abu Ishaq narrated to us from Abdurrahman ibn Yazid who said: We said to Hudhayfah: Tell us of a man close in guidance, manner and conduct to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so we may learn from him, he said: I know no one closer in manner, guidance and conduct to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), until the wall of his house conceals him, than Ibn Umm Abd."
"23808","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from al-A'mash, Shaqiq narrated to me from Hudhayfah who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a road, so he stepped aside and came to a rubbish heap of some people, so I moved away from him, then he drew me near until I was close to his heels, and he urinated standing and called for water and performed ablution and wiped over his khuffs."
"23809","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, and Abdurrahman from Sufyan from Mansur and Husayn from Abu Wa'il, Abdurrahman said, and al-A'mash from Abu Wa'il from Hudhayfah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he rose at night, and Waki' said: for tahajjud, would rub his mouth with the siwak."
"23810","Waki' narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated to us from Ibn Sirin who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and Hudhayfah met him, so he slipped away from him and bathed, then came, and he said: What is with you, he said: O Messenger of Allah, I was junub, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the Muslim does not become impure."
"23811","Waki' narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us from Wasil from Abu Wa'il from Hudhayfah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it, that he met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and slipped away from him and bathed, then came, he said: The Muslim does not become impure."
"23812","Waki' narrated to us from Ibn Abi Layla from a shaykh called Hilal from Hudhayfah who said: And I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about everything, even about leveling the pebbles, and he said: One time, or leave it."
"23813","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abdulmalik ibn Umayr from a freedman of Rib'i ibn Hirash from Rib'i ibn Hirash from Hudhayfah who said: We were sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: I do not know how long I shall remain among you, so follow the two after me, and he pointed to Abu Bakr and Umar, he said: And whatever Ibn Mas'ud narrates to you, believe him."
"23814","Waki' narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us from Ibrahim from Hammam from Hudhayfah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No tale-bearer shall enter Paradise."
"23815","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Ubayd ibn al-Mughirah from Hudhayfah who said: There was sharpness in my tongue against my family, and it did not go beyond them to others, so I complained of that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: So where are you with seeking forgiveness, O Hudhayfah, I seek forgiveness from Allah a hundred times a day."
"23816","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from Mansur who said: I heard Abu Wa'il narrating that Abu Musa was strict about urine, he said: When one of the Children of Israel was touched by urine he would follow it with scissors, Hudhayfah said: I wish he would not be strict, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) come, or he said: walk, to a rubbish heap of some people and urinate while standing."
"23817","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Hajjaj both said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Hammad from Rib'i from Hudhayfah who said, Shu'bah once raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah will bring out foul-smelling people whom the Fire has scorched, through the intercession of the intercessors, and admit them into Paradise, and they will be called the Jahannamis, Hajjaj said: the Jahannamin."
"23818","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from Hammad who said: I heard Rib'i ibn Hirash narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned it."
"23819","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu al-Tayyah who said: I heard Sakhr narrating from Subay' who said: They sent me from a watering place to Kufa to buy riding animals, so we came to al-Kunasah and there was a man wearing a cloak, as for my companion he went off to the animals, and as for me I went to him, and behold it was Hudhayfah, and I heard him saying: The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to ask him about good and I ask him about evil, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, is there after this good an evil as there was evil before it, he said: Yes, I said: So what is protection from it, he said: The sword, I think Abu al-Tayyah says: the sword, I think, he said: I said: Then what, he said: Then there will be a truce upon smoke, he said: I said: Then what, he said: Then there will be callers to misguidance, he said: If you then see Allah's caliph on earth, cling to him, even if he wears out your body and takes your wealth, and if you do not see him then flee in the land, even if you die biting the root of a tree, he said: I said: Then what, he said: Then the Dajjal will come out, he said: I said: With what will he come, with him, he said: With a river, or he said: water and fire, so whoever enters his river, his reward is lost and his burden becomes due, and whoever enters his fire, his reward becomes due and his burden is dropped, he said: I said: Then what, he said: If you bred a mare and did not ride its foal until the Hour comes, Shu'bah said, and Abu Bishr narrated to me with a chain of his from Hudhayfah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is a truce upon smoke, he said: Hearts that do not return to what they were."
"23820","Abdussamad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu al-Tayyah narrated to me, Sakhr ibn Badr al-Ijli narrated to me from Subay' ibn Khalid al-Duba'i, and he mentioned the like of its meaning, and said: And his reward is lost and his burden is dropped, he said: Even if he wears out your back and takes your wealth."
"23821","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us from Abu al-Tayyah from Sakhr from Subay' ibn Khalid al-Duba'i, and he mentioned it, and said: Even if he wears out your back and devours your wealth, and said: And his reward is lost and his burden is dropped."
"23822","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us from Qatadah from Nasr ibn Asim al-Laythi from Khalid ibn Khalid al-Yashkuri who said: I went out at the time Tustar was conquered until I came to Kufa, and I entered the mosque and there was a circle with a man of medium build among men, handsome in his smile, known in him to be from the men of the Hijaz, he said: So I said: Who is the man, so the people said: Do you not know him, I said: No, so they said: This is Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, the companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: So I sat and he narrated to the people and said: People used to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about good, and I used to ask him about evil, so the people disapproved of that from him, so he said to them: I shall tell you what you disapproved of that: Islam came when it came, and there came a matter unlike the matter of Jahiliyyah, and I had been given understanding in the Qur'an, and men would come asking about good, while I would ask him about evil, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, will there be after this good an evil as there was evil before it, so he said: Yes, he said: I said: So what is protection, O Messenger of Allah, he said: The sword, he said: I said: And is there after this sword any remnant, he said: Yes, there will be rule upon specks and a truce upon smoke, he said: I said: Then what, he said: Then callers to misguidance will arise, so if there is on that day a caliph of Allah on earth who lashes your back and takes your wealth, cling to him, otherwise die biting the root of a tree, he said: I said: Then what, he said: The Dajjal will come out after that, with him a river and a fire, whoever falls into his fire, his reward becomes due and his burden is dropped, and whoever falls into his river, his burden becomes due and his reward is lost, he said: I said: Then what, he said: Then the foal is bred and not ridden until the Hour comes. As-Sad' among men is the medium-built, and his saying 'so what is protection from it', he said: the sword, Qatadah used to apply it to the apostasy in the time of Abu Bakr, and his saying 'rule upon specks and a truce' means truce, and his saying 'upon smoke' means upon grudges. It was said to Abdurrazzaq: From whom is the explanation, he said: From Qatadah, he claimed."
"23823","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from Sulayman who said: I heard Zayd ibn Wahb narrating from Hudhayfah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us two hadiths, I have seen one of them and I am waiting for the other, and he mentioned the hadith."
"23824","Bahz narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us from Nasr ibn Asim from Subay' ibn Khalid who said: I came to Kufa at the time Tustar was conquered, and he mentioned the like of the meaning of Ma'mar's hadith, and said: His burden is dropped."
"23825","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Bakkar narrated to us, Khallad ibn Abdurrahman narrated to me that he heard Abu al-Tufayl narrating that he heard Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman saying: O people, will you not ask me, for people used to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about good and I used to ask him about evil, indeed Allah sent His Prophet, upon him prayer and peace, and called people from disbelief to faith and from misguidance to guidance, so whoever responded responded, and there lived through the truth what had been dead, and there died through falsehood what had been alive, then prophethood went and there was caliphate upon the way of prophethood."
"23826","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us from Abu Ishaq, one who was with Sa'id ibn al-As in a raid called the raid of al-Khashab narrated to me, and with him was Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, so Sa'id said: Which of you witnessed the fear prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so Hudhayfah said: I, he said: So Hudhayfah ordered them and they wore arms, then he said: If any disturbance alarms you, fighting has become lawful for you, he said: So he prayed one rak'ah with one of the two groups, while the other group faced the enemy, then these left and stood in the place of those, and those came and he prayed another rak'ah with them, then he greeted them."
"23827","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Mansur from Ibrahim from Hammam ibn al-Harith who said: We were with Hudhayfah and a man passed, and they said: This one conveys reports to the commanders, so he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No tale-bearer shall enter Paradise."
"23828","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Abduljabbar ibn al-Abbas al-Shami narrated to us from Abu Qays, Abduljabbar said: I think from Huzayl, who said: Hudhayfah stood as a preacher in the house of Amir ibn Hanzalah, among them Tamimi and Mudari, and said: There shall come upon Mudar a day when they shall leave no servant of Allah worshipping Him but they kill him, or they shall surely be beaten such that they cannot protect the tail of a hill or the foot of a hill, so it was said: O Abu Abdillah, do you say this to your people, or to a people you are, meaning, from them, he said: I say, meaning, only what I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying."
"23829","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Isra'il informed us, Maysarah ibn Habib informed me from al-Minhal from Zirr ibn Hubaysh from Hudhayfah who said: My mother said to me: When is your meeting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: So I said: I have had no meeting with him for such and such, he said: So she scolded me, I said: O mother, leave me until I go to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I shall not leave him until he seeks forgiveness for me and seeks forgiveness for you, he said: So I came to him and prayed Maghrib with him, and when he finished the prayer he stood praying, and he kept praying until he prayed Isha, then he went out."
"23830","Abdulaziz ibn Abdussamad narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us from Mujahid from Abdurrahman ibn Abi Layla from Hudhayfah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to drink in vessels of gold and silver, and to eat in them, and to wear silk and brocade, and said: They are for them in this world and for you in the Hereafter."
"23831","Yazid narrated to us, Hajjaj informed us from Abdurrahman ibn Abis from his father from Hudhayfah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever stipulates for his brother a condition he does not intend to fulfill for him, he is like one who lets his neighbor down to no protection."
"23832","Yazid narrated to us, Hajjaj informed us from Abdurrahman ibn Abis from his father from Hudhayfah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever stipulates for his brother a condition he does not intend to fulfill for him, he is like one who lets his neighbor down to no protection."
"23833","Yazid narrated to us, Abu Malik informed us from Rib'i ibn Hirash from Hudhayfah that he came from Umar, he said: When we sat with him, he asks the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which of you heard the statement of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about tribulations, they said: We heard it, he said: Perhaps you mean the tribulation of a man in his family and wealth, they said: Yes, he said: That is not what I ask about, those are expiated by prayer, fasting and charity, but which of you heard the statement of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the tribulations that surge as the sea surges, he said: So the people fell silent, and I thought he meant me, he said: I said: I have it, he said: You are for Allah, your father, he said: I said: Tribulations are presented to hearts like a mat, so any heart that rejects them, a white dot is marked in it, and any heart that is gladdened by them, a black dot is marked in it, until hearts become upon two hearts: white like Safa, no tribulation harms it as long as the heavens and earth endure, and the other black and dusty like an overturned vessel, and he tilted his palm, recognizing no right nor denying any wrong except what was steeped of its whim, and I told him that between him and it is a closed door about to be broken with a breaking, Umar said: A breaking, no father for you, he said: I said: Yes, he said: If it were opened, it might be restored and closed, he said: I said: No, rather a breaking, he said: And I told him that that door is a man who will be killed or die, a hadith with no confusion."
"23834","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Malik informed us, Rib'i ibn Hirash narrated to me from Hudhayfah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All good conduct is charity, and the last that the people of Jahiliyyah clung to of the speech of prophethood: If you feel no shame, do what you wish."
"23835","Yazid narrated to us, Sharik ibn Abdillah informed us from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud from Zirr ibn Hubaysh who said: I said, meaning to Hudhayfah: O Abu Abdillah, did you take suhur with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Yes, I said: Could a man see the places of his arrows, he said: Yes, it is daytime, except that the sun had not risen."
"23836","Rawh and Affan both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Asim ibn Bahdalah from Zirr ibn Hubaysh from Hudhayfah who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying in a lane of the lanes of Madinah: I am Muhammad, and I am Ahmad, and al-Hashir, and al-Muqaffa, and the Prophet of mercy."
"23837","Amr ibn Asim narrated to us from Hammad ibn Salamah from Ali ibn Zayd from al-Hasan from Jundub from Hudhayfah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: It is not fitting for a Muslim to humiliate himself, it was said: And how does he humiliate himself, he said: He exposes himself to a trial he cannot bear."
"23838","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us from Asim from Abu Wa'il who said: Hudhayfah said: While I was walking on a road of Madinah, he said: Behold the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walking, and I heard him saying: I am Muhammad, and I am Ahmad, and the Prophet of mercy, and the Prophet of repentance, and al-Hashir, and al-Muqaffa, and the Prophet of battles."
"23839","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Isra'il informed us from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, al-Mughirah ibn Hadhf narrated to me from Hudhayfah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shared a cow among the Muslims on behalf of seven."
"23840","Abdussamad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us from Asim from Zirr from Hudhayfah that Jibril, peace be upon him, met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the stones of al-Mira', and said: O Jibril, I have been sent to an unlettered ummah, to the old man and the old woman, and the boy and the girl, and the elder who never read a book at all, so he said: The Qur'an was sent down upon seven ahruf."
"23841","Abdussamad narrated to us, Abdulaziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdillah al-Jabir narrated to us who said: I prayed behind Isa, a freedman of Hudhayfah, at al-Mada'in over a funeral, and he said takbir five times, then he turned to us and said: I neither erred nor forgot, but I said takbir as my master and benefactor Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman said takbir, he prayed over a funeral and said takbir five times, then he turned to us and said: I neither forgot nor erred, but I said takbir as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said takbir, he prayed over a funeral and said takbir five times."
"23842","Abdussamad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us from al-Yashkuri from Hudhayfah who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, is there after this good an evil as there was evil before it, he said: O Hudhayfah, read the Book of Allah and act by what is in it, so he turned away from me, so I repeated to him three times, and I knew that if it were good I would follow it, and if it were evil I would avoid it, so I said: Is there after this good any evil, he said: Yes, a blind, dark, deaf tribulation, and callers to misguidance at the gates of Jahannam, whoever answers them they hurl him into it."
"23843","Abdussamad narrated to us from Mahdi from Wasil from Abu Wa'il from Hudhayfah that word reached him that a man spreads reports, so Hudhayfah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No slanderer shall enter Paradise."
"23844","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Asim from Zirr from Hudhayfah who said: The Hawd of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the Day of Resurrection, its drink is whiter than milk, sweeter than honey, colder than snow, and more fragrant than musk, and its vessels are as many as the stars of the sky."
"23845","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Kathir ibn Abi Kathir informed us, Rib'i ibn Hirash narrated to us from Hudhayfah that a man came to him at al-Mada'in, so Hudhayfah said to him: What did your people do, he said: I said: About which of their concerns do you ask, he said: Who went out from them to this man, meaning Uthman, he said: I said: So-and-so and so-and-so and so-and-so, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever leaves the community and belittles the leadership shall meet Allah, mighty and majestic, with no standing with Him."
"23846","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Utaybah narrated to us from al-Mughirah ibn Hadhf from Hudhayfah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shared in his Hajj a cow among the Muslims on behalf of seven."
"23847","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Sulaym ibn Abd al-Saluli who said: We were with Sa'd ibn al-As at Tabaristan, and with him a group of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Which of you prayed the fear prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so Hudhayfah said: I, so order your companions to stand in two groups, a group behind you and a group facing the enemy, so you say takbir and they say takbir together, then you bow and they bow together, then you rise and they rise together, then you prostrate and the group next to you prostrates with you, while the group facing the enemy stands facing the enemy, so when you raise your head from prostration they prostrate, then these move back and the others advance and stand in their ranks, so you bow and they bow together, then you prostrate and the group next to you prostrates, while the other group stands facing the enemy, so when you raise your head from prostration they prostrate, then you give salam and some of them give salam to some, and order your companions that if any disturbance of the enemy alarms them, fighting and speech have become lawful for them."
"23848","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Habib ibn Sulaym al-Absi narrated to us from Bilal al-Absi from Hudhayfah that when one of his dead died he would say: Do not announce it to anyone, I fear it may be wailing announcement, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding wailing announcement."
"23849","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Umar ibn Muhammad from Umar, freedman of Ghufrah, from a man of the Ansar from Hudhayfah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every ummah has Magians, and the Magians of this ummah are those who say there is no decree, so if any of them falls sick do not visit him, and if any of them dies do not attend him, and they are the party of the Dajjal, it is due upon Allah, mighty and majestic, to join them with him."
"23850","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us from Amr ibn Murrah from Abu al-Bakhtari from Hudhayfah who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at a funeral, and when we reached the grave he sat at its edge and kept turning his gaze in it, then he said: The believer is squeezed in it with a squeeze from which his carriers shift, and it is filled with fire upon the disbeliever, then he said: Shall I not tell you of the worst of Allah's servants, the harsh, the arrogant, shall I not tell you of the best of Allah's servants, the weak, the deemed weak, with two worn garments, if he swore by Allah, Allah would fulfill his oath."
"23851","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to me from Husayn who said: I heard Abu Wa'il narrating from Hudhayfah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he rose for tahajjud would rub his mouth with the siwak."
"23852","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us from Abdulmalik ibn Umayr from Rib'i ibn Hirash from Hudhayfah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he went to his bed would say: In Your name, O Allah, I die and I live, and when he woke he would say: Praise be to Allah who gave us life after He made us die, and to Him is the resurrection."
"23853","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said, and Shu'ayb is I, from al-Zuhri who said: Abu Idris A'idhullah ibn Abdillah al-Khawlani would say: I heard Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman saying: By Allah, I know every tribulation occurring before the Hour, and it is not that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) confided to me about that anything he did not tell another, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said while narrating in a gathering I was in about tribulations, he said, while counting them, among them three that hardly leave anything, and among them tribulations like summer winds, among them small and among them great, Hudhayfah said: So all that group went except me."
"23854","Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us from Abu Wa'il from Hudhayfah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he rose at night would rub his mouth with the siwak."
"23855","Mus'ab ibn Sallam narrated to us, al-Ajlah narrated to us from Qays ibn Abi Muslim from Rib'i ibn Hirash who said: I heard Hudhayfah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck for us parables: one, three, five, seven, nine and eleven, he said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck for us one parable of them and left the rest, he said: A people were weak and poor, and people of tyranny and numbers fought them, so Allah gave the weak victory over them, then they turned to their enemy and employed them and gave them power, so they earned Allah's anger upon them until the day they meet Him."
"23856","Mus'ab ibn Sallam narrated to us, al-Ajlah narrated to us from Nu'aym ibn Abi Hind from Rib'i ibn Hirash who said: I sat with Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman and Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, one of them said to the other: Narrate what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No, rather you narrate, so one of them narrated to his companion and the other confirmed him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, and Allah will say: Look into his deed, so he will say: My Lord, I never did any good except that I had wealth and I dealt with people, so whoever was well-off I eased for him, and whoever was in hardship I granted him respite until ease, Allah, mighty and majestic, will say: I am most entitled to ease, so He forgave him, so he said: You spoke true, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying this."
"23857","Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection who had said to his family: When I die, burn me, then grind me, then face with me a stormy wind and scatter me, so Allah, blessed and exalted, will gather him on the Day of Resurrection and say to him: Why did you do it, he will say: From fear of You, so He will forgive him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying it."
"23858","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ziyad narrated to us from Abdurrahman ibn Abi Layla who said: I was with Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman at al-Mada'in, and he asked for drink, so a dihqan brought him a vessel, so he threw it at him, hardly missing striking his face with it, then he said: Were it not that I had warned him once or twice I would not have done this with him, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to drink in vessels of gold and silver, and to wear silk and brocade, he said: It is for them in this world and for us in the Hereafter. This is the end of the hadith of Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, may Allah be pleased with him."
